<script>
import Code from '#src/lib/Code.abide'
import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
</script>

<Doc
    seeAlso={['/reactive/memo', '/reactive/refresh']}
    tests={[
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/stopSignal.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('stopSignal in a memo body is its run’s own, ended by the next run — 7.45, 7.46'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/stopSignal.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('stopSignal is aborted from the stop through its drain, and fresh once the stop resolves — 7.38, 7.39'",
            ],
        },
        {
            path: 'packages/abide/tests/stopSignal.test.ts',
            from: [
                "test('a job giving up on stopSignal is not warned on, and a failing one still is — 4.12, 7.28, 37.28'",
            ],
        },
    ]}
>
    <Section level={3} title="Cancel a search the next keystroke replaces">
        <p>Inside a <code>memo</code> body the signal is that run's own. The next run aborts it, so
            the search a keystroke made obsolete stops rather than finishing for nobody.</p>
        <Code language="abide" caption="abide" code={`
            <script>
            import { memo, reactive, stopSignal } from '@abide/abide'

            let q = reactive('')
            const found = memo(() =>
                fetch(\`/search?q=\${q}\`, { signal: stopSignal() }).then((r) => r.json()),
            )
            </script>

            <input bind:value={q}>
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="End a follow-up sweep when the app stops">
        <p>A job on a clock can run for a while. Read <code>stopSignal()</code> in its run and
            stop early, rather than holding the shutdown until the sweep ends.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { memo, stopSignal } from '@abide/abide'
            import { DEALS } from '../../pipeline/lib/DEALS.server.ts'

            export const followUps = memo(
                async function* () {
                    const stopping = stopSignal()
                    for (const deal of DEALS) {
                        if (stopping.aborted) return
                        await Bun.sleep(1) // a look at the lead's inbox
                        if (deal.stage === 'lead') yield deal.name
                    }
                },
                { global: true, poll: 300_000 },
            )
        `} />
    </Section>

    <Section level={3} title="Cancel a request the job has in flight">
        <p>The signal is an <code>AbortSignal</code>, so hand it to <code>fetch</code> and the
            stop cancels the request too.</p>
        <Code language="ts" caption="server" code={`
            import { stopSignal } from '@abide/abide'

            const reply = await fetch(INBOX_URL, { signal: stopSignal() })
        `} />
    </Section>
</Doc>
